WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.425
This is Allen Company training on abandoned areas

00:07.425 --> 00:10.525
underground, and on barricading as a last resort

00:10.525 --> 00:13.513
in an emergency. Abandoned or worked-out areas

00:13.513 --> 00:17.425
can hold bad air, low oxygen, loose roof and ribs,

00:17.425 --> 00:20.712
and water. They aren't examined like active areas.

00:21.828 --> 00:24.503
Hazardous areas are barricaded, or posted with

00:24.503 --> 00:27.466
warning signs at every approach that can be seen.

00:27.466 --> 00:30.266
Never go past a barricade or a danger sign unless

00:30.266 --> 00:32.191
you've been assigned and trained to,

00:32.191 --> 00:34.041
and the area has been examined.

00:35.204 --> 00:37.604
Here's what one looks like at Boonesboro:

00:37.604 --> 00:40.491
part of 2 West, on the way toward the Liwell plant

00:40.491 --> 00:43.179
and the roll crusher, is blocked off with posts

00:43.179 --> 00:46.328
and a warning sign. Every mine has its own map,

00:46.328 --> 00:48.791
and the areas that are blocked off or no longer

00:48.791 --> 00:51.779
worked change as mining moves. Your instructor

00:51.779 --> 00:53.766
will show you where they are on your mine's current

00:53.766 --> 00:55.991
map, and how they're marked underground,

00:55.991 --> 00:57.141
on your mine tour.

01:00.472 --> 01:04.022
In a fire, your first job is always to escape,

01:04.022 --> 01:06.697
by your primary escapeway or your secondary if

01:06.697 --> 01:09.872
the first is blocked. Barricading is only for when

01:09.872 --> 01:11.697
every way out is cut off.

01:12.838 --> 01:15.551
If miners can't reach the surface through two separate

01:15.551 --> 01:18.288
escapeways within an hour, the mine must provide

01:18.288 --> 01:21.239
a method of refuge. None of Allen's mines has a

01:21.239 --> 01:24.239
designated refuge, and Allen does not barricade

01:24.239 --> 01:27.038
as a planned method, so no barricading materials

01:27.038 --> 01:29.901
are kept on site. Escape is the plan.

01:31.025 --> 01:33.437
What follows is general awareness only,

01:33.437 --> 01:36.262
not an Allen procedure, in case you ever work somewhere

01:36.262 --> 01:39.087
that uses it. If miners must barricade:

01:39.087 --> 01:41.700
they pick a spot with the best air you can find,

01:41.700 --> 01:44.900
as much space as possible, away from the smoke.

01:44.900 --> 01:47.550
They build the barricade with whatever is at hand,

01:47.550 --> 01:50.087
such as posts and brattice cloth, and seal the

01:50.087 --> 01:53.112
edges with fine rock or dust. They leave a sign

01:53.112 --> 01:55.687
outside saying who is inside and when they went

01:55.687 --> 01:58.287
in, and build a second curtain for an air lock

01:58.287 --> 01:59.287
if they can.

02:00.406 --> 02:03.869
Inside, stay calm, stay still to save air,

02:03.869 --> 02:06.556
use one light at a time, and keep your self-rescuer

02:06.556 --> 02:09.569
ready. Rescuers listen for tapping on pipes or

02:09.569 --> 02:12.744
roof bolts at intervals. Allen has no set signaling

02:12.744 --> 02:16.306
procedure, so follow the mine rescue team's instructions.

02:17.440 --> 02:20.465
Recap: stay out of abandoned and blocked-off areas

02:20.465 --> 02:23.090
and never cross a barricade or danger sign.

02:23.090 --> 02:26.465
Escape first, by either escapeway. At Allen,

02:26.465 --> 02:29.890
escape is the plan. Barricading is general awareness

02:29.890 --> 02:32.252
only, a last resort elsewhere.

02:33.370 --> 02:36.532
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

02:36.532 --> 02:38.033
override this video.
